### Skip invalid persisted grid and canvas geometry

**Severity:** `high`

`FromCustomLayouts` currently returns deserialized entries without checking their geometry. A persisted grid with a missing `cell-child-map` becomes an empty map here, although the native reader rejects it. Validate the converted grid or canvas with the existing validators before adding it; warn and skip invalid entries so `get`/`export` do not report that grid as a usable layout. This targeted block does not address missing names or omitted canvas coordinates; cover those separately. A malformed persisted-grid regression should produce a warning and no returned layout.

```suggestion
            var validationErrors = new List<string>();
            if (entry.Grid != null)
            {
                ValidateGrid(entry.Grid, "grid", validationErrors);
            }
            else if (entry.Canvas != null)
            {
                ValidateCanvas(entry.Canvas, "canvas", validationErrors);
            }

            if (validationErrors.Count > 0)
            {
                warnings?.Add($"Skipping custom layout '{uuid}' with invalid layout info: {string.Join("; ", validationErrors)}");
                continue;
            }

            result.Add(entry);
```

### Accumulate grid percentages without Int32 overflow

**Severity:** `medium`

`ValidatePercentages` accumulates positive `int` values into an `int` before comparing to `10000`. For `[2147483647,2147483647,10002]`, unchecked addition wraps to `10000`, so an invalid input can pass. Widen the accumulator and format the widened diagnostic together in this one block: changing the declaration alone does not compile against the existing `Invariant(int)` helper. The focused regression should reject that input and report `4294977296`.

```suggestion
        long sum = 0;
        for (var i = 0; i < values.Count; i++)
        {
            if (values[i] <= 0)
            {
                errors.Add($"{context}[{Invariant(i)}] must be greater than 0");
            }

            sum += values[i];
        }

        if (sum != PercentageTotal)
        {
            errors.Add($"{context} must sum to {Invariant(PercentageTotal)} (100.00%) but sums to {sum.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)}");
```

### Reject disconnected grid regions without rejecting gapped IDs

**Severity:** `high`

`ValidateGrid` accepts `[[0,1],[1,0]]`, but the native builder encounters the same zone ID at separate top-left positions and `AddZone` rejects the duplicate. Require each used ID to occupy one rectangle after checking row shape. Do not require IDs to be contiguous: `[0,2,2]` is not rejected by the native builder merely because ID 1 is absent. Cover both examples in regression tests.

```suggestion
        }

        if (cellChildMap.Any(cells => cells == null || cells.Count != grid.Columns))
        {
            return;
        }

        foreach (var zoneIndex in cellChildMap.SelectMany(row => row).Distinct())
        {
            var cells = cellChildMap
                .SelectMany((row, rowIndex) => row.Select((value, columnIndex) => (value, rowIndex, columnIndex)))
                .Where(cell => cell.value == zoneIndex)
                .ToList();
            var minRow = cells.Min(cell => cell.rowIndex);
            var maxRow = cells.Max(cell => cell.rowIndex);
            var minColumn = cells.Min(cell => cell.columnIndex);
            var maxColumn = cells.Max(cell => cell.columnIndex);
            for (var row = minRow; row <= maxRow; row++)
            {
                for (var column = minColumn; column <= maxColumn; column++)
                {
                    if (cellChildMap[row][column] != zoneIndex)
                    {
                        errors.Add($"{mapContext}: zone index {Invariant(zoneIndex)} must form a single rectangle");
                        return;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
```

### Reject unknown nested input properties (1/2)

**Severity:** `medium`

Apply both parts together. The structural checks validate section names and entry kinds, but default deserialization silently ignores nested typos such as `zoneCounnt`. Cache strict serializer options rather than allocating a new options object for every command; part 2 uses this instance. A valid `zoneCount` must still be accepted.

```suggestion
    public const string DefaultLayoutsFileName = "default-layouts.json";

    private static readonly JsonSerializerOptions _inputSerializerOptions = new()
    {
        UnmappedMemberHandling = System.Text.Json.Serialization.JsonUnmappedMemberHandling.Disallow,
    };
```

### Warn for a missing stored custom-layout array (1/2)

**Severity:** `medium`

Apply both parts together. A present `{}` wrapper becomes an empty custom list without a warning, although the native parser requires `custom-layouts`. Report the missing array before returning empty state. Part 2 prevents this check from adding warnings for absent files or duplicating an existing malformed-JSON warning. Literal `null` already follows the malformed-JSON warning path and is not a new defect.

```suggestion
        var result = new List<FzCustomLayout>();
        if (stored.CustomLayouts == null)
        {
            warnings?.Add("custom-layouts.json is malformed and is treated as empty: expected a top-level 'custom-layouts' array");
            return result;
        }
```

### Warn for a missing stored custom-layout array (2/2)

**Severity:** `medium`

Apply both parts together. Read the custom file first, then pass the warning collector only when the file is present and `ReadFile` did not already report malformed JSON. This preserves silent empty state for missing files and exactly one warning for malformed files, while allowing part 1 to warn for a present `{}` wrapper. Existing invalid-entry warnings remain enabled for successfully read files.

```suggestion
        var customLayouts = ReadFile(new CustomLayouts(), CustomLayoutsFileName);
        var reportCustomWarnings = File.Exists(Path.Combine(DataFolder(), CustomLayoutsFileName)) &&
            !Warnings.Any(warning => warning.StartsWith($"{CustomLayoutsFileName} is malformed", StringComparison.Ordinal));
        layouts.Custom = FzLayoutsConverter.FromCustomLayouts(customLayouts, reportCustomWarnings ? Warnings : null);
```
